df <- run_range_wide_iucn(n_runs=200, n_cores=8,
                           results_dir="results/range_wide_iucn/")
plot_range_wide_iucn(df, save_path="outputs/range_wide_iucn.png")

Three design notes worth flagging:

Resistance hook — there's a clearly marked # RESISTANCE HOOK comment in build_site_params(). When you have site-level resistance data, add a resist_freq0 column to mn_site_params.csv and uncomment the one line. No structural changes needed.

Site metadata join — the run_id hash lets us join site information back to results after the fact. The join works by reconstructing the site-seed mapping from the same random seed (42), so it's deterministic even after restarts.

The scatter plot — Panel C (fire × rust interaction surface) is the most scientifically interesting output. It directly shows whether the high-fire + high-rust corner produces categorically different outcomes from the low-fire + low-rust corner, which speaks directly to the synergism question that's central to this work.

